1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Next, add a copy of the D-circle to the back of the model.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Open the copy of Connect, select the hardware, and select Rings.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Find the D-circle.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Double-click to add to the object window.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Drag the D-circle from the object window to the 3D window.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
In the open copy window, you can choose the location of the D-circle,

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
the original location or the location of the coordinate 0, 0.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Here, select the original location and the location when the D-circle is stored.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Use the move tool to select the D-circle.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
There are three tools in the upper right corner.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Next, we will apply these three tools.

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
First, single-click to start the first quick arrangement tool.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
When the mouse moves on the costume,

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
you can see the gray shadow of the D-circle moving with the mouse,

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
and it is in the position where the D-circle moves.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
When you come to the location near the target,

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,000
you can easily and quickly place the D-circle near the target location.

18
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Again, single-click to start the third glue tool.

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
In the appropriate position,

20
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
single-click to move the D-circle to this position.

21
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
You can use the positioning ball to slightly move the D-circle.

22
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
In the object window, select the D-circle component,

23
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
and in the property editor,

24
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,000
select its specification property.

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
First, you can enter the name of the component,

26
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
product number, and other information.

27
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The proportion in the specification can be adjusted

28
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
to the size of the component in the X, Y, and Z axis.

29
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
The default fixed proportion is used.

30
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
You can adjust the size according to the proportion.

31
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
In the weight column, set the weight of the component.

32
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
The input weight value will be reflected in the simulation.

33
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Under the material, you can set the material type of the component.

34
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
In addition, there is another way to adjust the size of the component.

35
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
After selecting the component with the move tool,

36
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,000
single-click on this square icon.

37
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
The coordinates are changed to the shrink adjustment coordinates.

38
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
The mouse is placed on the red, green, blue coordinate axis separately.

39
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
When the left key is pressed and the mouse is moved,

40
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
the size of the corresponding direction of the component can be changed.

41
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
If you want to increase or decrease the proportion,

42
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
put the mouse on the left mouse button.

43
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
In this way,

44
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
the mouse is placed on the gray, three-dimensional square in the middle.

45
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
The mouse is changed to a diagonal arrowhead.

46
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
The left key is pressed and moved,

47
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
and the proportion can be reduced according to the size of the component.

48
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
After adjusting the size,

49
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
single-click on the icon to close this coordinate.

50
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
The terrain ring is in the selected state.

51
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,000
The property editor can edit its conflict thickness and rigidity.

52
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
The component simulation is carried out below.

53
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
The component simulation can carry out the movement of the B pin,

54
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
and interact stably with the 3D clothing.

55
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Before simulation,

56
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
right-click on the component first,

57
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
to ensure that the activation is activated.

58
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Then,

59
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
click to simulate.

60
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,000
You can see the terrain ring collides and simulate between the panels naturally.

61
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,000
After stabilization,

62
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
close the simulation.

63
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
The terrain ring is added and completed.

64
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Right-click on the terrain ring again.

65
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
The simulation column is removed from the activation.

66
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
There are two other options.

67
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Freeze and Reactivate.

68
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
For the component,

69
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
if you only want it to collide with the panel,

70
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
and not move,

71
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,000
select Freeze.

72
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
If you want to stop the collision and simulate at the same time,

73
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
select Reactivate.

74
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Finally, the completed component will be saved.

75
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Select it in the object window.

76
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
In the property editor,

77
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
click Save.

78
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Save the component in the .trm file format,

79
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
so that it can be used later.

80
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Now,

81
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:03,000
model a state of the area .

82
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Select this state.

83
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Go back to the model .

84
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Select the .trm function.

85
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Select the .trm object from the .trm tutorial.

86
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Select .

87
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Select .trm .

88
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Click .

